    "text": "Everything I ate in Berlin Part 2!! I will also be doing video on matcha spots soon so stay tuned for that!! Places mentioned: \n- trio\n- wen cheng\n- romeo’s sandwiches \n- markthalle food hall\n- khinkali station \n#berlin #foodtok #foodreview #berlinfood #berlinfoodguide ",
    "subtitles": "Here's everything I ate in Berlin part 2.\nAs a half German girl\nwho didn't really eat much German food growing up,\ntrio was such a fantastic meal.\nThey do modern takes on traditional German dishes.\nAs soon as I saw Ella eat said this was their favourite meal in Berlin,\nI really wanted to try it and it was so worth it.\nWe were really craving Asian food so we thought we try Wen Cheng.\nWe had the lamb and cumin bian bian noodles.\nFlavour and portioning were great,\nbut when I had the dumplings in the bowl\nI did think I've had better back home.\nOverall though, this definitely did satisfy that craving.\nI loved the tuna melt and the chicken Caesar from Romeo's.\nThey were packed with flavour and really filling.\nThey had the most incredible kesserschmettla at Magdalena.\nI thought this market had some really unique cuisines and options.\nIt's worth checking out for sure.\nLast meal before flying were these\nJordan dumplings and acharuli at King Kelly Station.\nNever had either of these before\nbut I'm already desperate to have them again.\nA whole video on matcha spots is coming soon\nand I'm gonna be making a more in depth video for YouTube\nif you'd like to see more food I tried in Berlin.",
    "subtitlesLanguage": "eng-US",
